# Names only. Never put real values in this file; real values go in .env.local (git-ignored)
# and in Vercel/Supabase environment settings.
#
# Safe for the browser (public by design; access is enforced by RLS):
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# The project this app may talk to; the app refuses any other (a stray production .env cannot be used by accident):
# RIO_SUPABASE_ALLOWED_REF=<20-character ref of the project, or "local" for a local stack>
# Public address of the admin panel (a separate site), used for the "Staff login" links. No trailing slash. Unset keeps the links on this origin.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ADMIN_URL=https://admin.example.org
# Server-only Express integration. The backend origin is never sent to browser code.
# RIO_API_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:4000
# RIO_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000
#
# Server only. Never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_ and never commit. Video upload (M4A) stays disabled until the secret key
# and all four R2 settings are set. The R2 key is scoped to the one private bucket (no public domain). The secret key is
# used only to call the upload functions after the parent's own session has been checked:
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=<server-only secret key; bypasses RLS, used only by trusted server code>
# Cloudflare R2 (private bucket, no public domain). Put the real values in .env.local, never in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ name:
# R2_ACCOUNT_ID=<32-character Cloudflare account id>
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=<R2 API token access key id, scoped to the one bucket>
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=<R2 API token secret access key>
# R2_BUCKET_NAME=<bucket name, lowercase letters, digits and hyphens>
# Check them without any network call or printed value:  npm run r2:check
# Master switch for video upload (M4A.1). Server-only. ONLY the exact value "yes" turns uploads on; missing, empty or any
# other value means OFF, in the page, in authorization and in confirmation. Keep it "no" until migration 00500 is applied,
# the bucket CORS is set and a real upload test is approved:
# RIO_UPLOADS_ENABLED=no
# Master switch for FINAL SUBMISSION (M4B). Server-only. ONLY the exact value "yes" turns it on; missing, empty or any other
# value means OFF, in the page, in the server action and when its dependencies are built. Keep it "no": an equal ETag does not
# prove what a video contains, so final submission must stay off until server-side media inspection exists (release blocker B1),
# migration 00600 has been applied, and the owner has approved. It is separate from the upload switch above.
# RIO_FINALIZE_ENABLED=no
# Confirmation e-mail after a final submission (M7). Server-only. Sending stays OFF until RIO_EMAIL_ENABLED is exactly "yes" AND the provider is configured and
# the owner has tested it. Until then the intention is only recorded in the outbox (after migration 00800), and nothing is sent. Nothing here is NEXT_PUBLIC.
# RIO_EMAIL_ENABLED=no
# EMAIL_PROVIDER=resend
# EMAIL_API_KEY=<the provider's API key, sending permission only>
# EMAIL_FROM=Rio Hospital <noreply@your-verified-domain>   (a sender on a domain verified with the provider: SPF and DKIM)
# EMAIL_REPLY_TO=<optional reply address>
# CRON_SECRET=<random string of at least 32 characters; the scheduler sends it as a Bearer token to /api/email-sweep to retry failed e-mails>
#
# Length of the email one-time code. Server-only, optional; unset means 6, allowed 6 to 10.
# It must equal the OTP length of the Supabase project this environment talks to (Authentication, Providers, Email).
# Set it per environment (.env.local for dev, Vercel settings for production). A wrong value stops sign-in; it never guesses.
# RIO_OTP_LENGTH=6
